  "description": "The new generation of Big Al, our gravity led hardcore alloy 29er. With hardtails being pushed harder and faster than ever before we have tweaked the trusted Ragley recipe for modern tastes. Our bikes have always been at the forefront of fun versatile hardcore hardtails and with a sprinkle of love with the same Ragley ingredients the fun has now been cranked up to 11.\nStriking a balance between hardcore capabilities and all-day riding. The Big AL headtube has now been slackened to 63.5˚ and complimented with a shorter seattube to drop your saddle further, giving you even more commanding control when the trail gets steep and rowdy. An increased reach and 5mm lower BB gives you highspeed confidence and technical stability. Then for when you bang the saddle back up, the steeper 75˚ seat-angle puts you in a comfortable, balanced and efficient pedalling position. More control and more fun like no other, with the updated geometry and 29’’ wheels the Big Al is at home being piloted at an Enduro Race, epics into the mountains, sweet flat-out singletrack and smashing laps at your favourite trail centre or bike park. The Big Al frame features all the modern no-nonsense fitting standards for easy serviceability. ISCG05 tabs, 44/56mm headtube, internal dropper routing, threaded BB and Boost 148x12mm rear wheel fitting. Engineered from custom butted 6061 Alloy tubing, offering a robust responsive frame but with balanced compliance and comfort.",
